  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1202 AM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nNot much change in the weather through the remainder of the weekend \nthrough late week. The boundary that comes through later Saturday \nwill bring temperatures down a few degrees for Sunday, and MAY \nproduce a few showers over the CONTDVD region during the afternoon \nSunday, otherwise it will be dry. Expect temps to be in the pleasant \n70s across the region on Sunday.\n\nFor all of next week, Mainly dry weather is expected. Only some \nscattered showers/storms could occur over the higher terrain during \nthe Tuesday time frame. Over the plains, max temps Will generally be \nin the lower to mid 80s, with the warmest day on the plains expected \nTuesday. Over the CONTDVD region will be consistent through Tuesday, \nbut from Wednesday onward, temps are forecast to gradually cool into \nthe weekend. \n\nBy late Saturday, statistical guidance is showing the beginning of a \ncooler trend as there is a much larger spread in the temps over all \nof the CWA on this day. Also POPs start to increase over the mtns by \nlate Saturday.\n\nLooking beyond this period, we may get some active weather into the \nregion by early next week (beyond OCT 11th). \\/Hodanish",
